{
 "format": 1,
 "what": "The voxel p99.9 stress of the stress report (`topopt.stress_report`) against the P2 p99.9 of `topopt verify`, on 5 public parts: the hook, the bracket, the ladle, and a shelf bracket and a phone stand made with the part builder. 51 cells (part x load case x run type). A measurement only: no code changed.",
 "issue": "chartergroup/topopt#129 (F1-8, step 1)",
 "main": "74a1e46",
 "host": "one shared Linux x86_64 host (PARDISO, 8 threads, one job at a time); not Apple silicon",
 "date": "2026-10-25",
 "script": "bench/stress_public_parts.py",
 "run_folders": "not in the repository. The cells below are the data. The 24 runs of the hook, the bracket and the ladle come from the F1-3 series (main d5002a4); the other runs were made on main 74a1e46. The shelf bracket and the phone stand are built from the specs in `bench/stress_public_parts_specs/` (`python -m topopt.regions_builder SPEC --out DIR`).",
 "definitions": {
  "voxel_value": "`metrics.stress.cases.<case>.independent_check.voxel_p99_9_by_volume_MPa`: the p99.9 by volume of the GREY design (the SIMP snapshot as the optimizer ran it; full E; hex8 centre; voxels with rho >= 0.5 in the peak scope)",
  "p2_value": "`verify/verify.json` `cases.<case>.von_mises.p99_9_by_volume_MPa`: `topopt verify` at its default mesh size (tets of final.stl, quadratic elements, all tets count)",
  "p2_over_voxel": "P2 / voxel (`independent_check.p2_over_voxel`). Above 1 the voxel value is below P2. A cell with a repeat run holds the mean of the two ratios, and the mean of the two values",
  "voxel_error_pct": "100 * (voxel / P2 - 1) = 100 * (1 / p2_over_voxel - 1): the error of the voxel value against P2, as in the bench",
  "cell": "(part, case, run type, variant). The variants S1, S2 and S3 are other designs of the same part (other pass counts)",
  "run_types": {
   "R": "compliance objective with the volume row, no stress row",
   "CS": "compliance objective with the volume row and stress rows (0.9 x the limits of MS)",
   "MS": "objective mass with stress rows, objective_scale stage",
   "MF": "as MS with objective_scale first"
  },
  "member_p10_voxels": "`member_check.p10_voxels` of the case: the estimated voxels through the member at the 1 % highest stress voxels",
  "thinnest_member_voxels": "`metrics.print.thinnest_member.thinnest_member_mm / voxel size` of the run",
  "near_share": "`verify.json` `von_mises.near_regions.top_volume_share_near.any`: the share of the P2 volume at or above its p99.9 that lies within 2 mm of a fixed or load region",
  "p2_peak_over_voxel_peak": "P2 peak at the quadrature points over the voxel peak (`peak_qp_over_voxel_peak`)",
  "grayness_last_pass": "`history.jsonl` key `grayness` of the last pass"
 },
